{"id":"3a9f5e4da7181cd37c8fde05b9aa06bd257107fa","axis":"silent","repo":"apache/tika","sha":"3a9f5e4da7181cd37c8fde05b9aa06bd257107fa","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"CHANGES.txt","lines":["@@ -1,5 +1,9 @@"," Release 4.2.0 - unreleased"," ","+   * The file-system emitter can gzip its output (\"compression\": \"GZIP\"), and tika-eval","+     finds gzipped extracts (.json.gz) when comparing against a plain extract set, measuring","+     their extract lengths and -m/-n limits on uncompressed size (TIKA-4989).","+","    * tika-server activates catalog presets from the command line (--preset <name>, repeatable)","      and the environment (TIKA_PRESETS, comma-separated), the equivalent of \"<name>\": true in","      the config's presets, overriding the file's own entry for the name; a config file needs"],"additions":4,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/modules/ROOT/pages/pipes/plugins/filesystem.adoc","lines":["@@ -147,6 +147,10 @@ Writes parsed results as files under `basePath`. The relative output path is der"," |`atomicWrites`"," |`true`"," |Write each output to a sibling `<name>.<uuid>.tmp` and rename it into place. A reader of the output directory never sees a partial file, but it does see the tmp files: crawlers and watchers over the output directory must ignore `*.tmp`. A worker killed mid-write leaves its `.tmp` behind, and nothing sweeps them. The `onExists: EXCEPTION`/`SKIP` check runs immediately before the rename and is best-effort against two workers emitting the same key concurrently (last writer wins) -- give workers distinct emit keys if that matters. Set to `false` to write in place (one fewer rename per file; required on mounts without rename, e.g. mountpoint-s3). Init-time only.","+","+|`compression`","+|`NONE`","+|`GZIP` gzips each output and appends `.gz` to its name, after `fileExtension` (`a.pdf.json.gz`). Applies where `fileExtension` does: the JSON metadata list, and the text of `CONTENT_ONLY`; unpacked files are written as they are. Extracted text typically shrinks 5-8x, and tika-eval reads `.json.gz` extracts directly. Init-time only."," |==="," "," [#file-system-iterator]"],"additions":4,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"tika-eval/tika-eval-app/src/main/java/org/apache/tika/eval/app/EvalFilePaths.java","lines":["@@ -23,6 +23,8 @@"," import java.nio.file.Path;"," import java.util.Objects;"," ","+import org.apache.tika.eval.app.io.ExtractReader;","+"," /**","  * Simple struct to keep track of relative path of source file (","  * original binary file, e.g. /subdir/document1.doc)","@@ -45,7 +47,7 @@ public EvalFilePaths(Path relativeSourceFilePath, Path extractFile, long srcFile","     public EvalFilePaths(Path relativeSourceFilePath, Path extractFile) {","         if (extractFile != null && Files.isRegularFile(extractFile)) {","             try {","-                extractFileLength = Files.size(extractFile);","+                extractFileLength = ExtractReader.extractLength(extractFile);","             } catch (IOException e) {","                 //swallow ?","             }"],"additions":3,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"tika-eval/tika-eval-app/src/main/java/org/apache/tika/eval/app/ProfilerBase.java","lines":["@@ -43,6 +43,7 @@"," import org.apache.tika.eval.app.db.ColInfo;"," import org.apache.tika.eval.app.db.Cols;"," import org.apache.tika.eval.app.db.TableInfo;","+import org.apache.tika.eval.app.io.ExtractReader;"," import org.apache.tika.eval.app.io.ExtractReaderException;"," import org.apache.tika.eval.app.io.IDBWriter;"," import org.apache.tika.eval.app.io.PipesReport;","@@ -93,7 +94,7 @@ public abstract class ProfilerBase {","     private static final String CONTAINER_EXCEPTION_1X = \"X-TIKA\" + \":EXCEPTION:runtime\";","     private static final Logger LOG = LoggerFactory.getLogger(ProfilerBase.class);","     private static final String[] EXTRACT_EXTENSIONS = {\".json\", \".txt\", \"\"};","-    private static final String[] COMPRESSION_EXTENSIONS = {\"\", \".bz2\", \".g