(path, gzip, options),","+                StandardCharsets.UTF_8));","+    }","+","+    private static OutputStream newOutputStream(Path path, boolean gzip, OpenOption... options)","+            throws IOException {","+        OutputStream os = Files.newOutputStream(path, options);","+        return gzip ? gzip(os) : os;","+    }","+","+    static OutputStream gzip(OutputStream os) throws IOException {","+        try {","+            return new GZIPOutputStream(os, GZIP_BUFFER_SIZE) {","+                // JDK 17's close() skips closing os when finish() throws (e.g. disk full)","+                @Override","+                public void close() throws IOException {","+                    try (os) {","+                        super.close();","+                    }","+                }","+            };","+        } catch (IOException e) {","+            os.close();","+            throw e;","+        }","+    }","+","     private static Path tmpFor(Path output) {","         // sibling so the rename stays on one filesystem (and therefore atomic)","         return output.resolveSibling(output.getFileName() + \".\" + UUID.randomUUID() + TMP_SUFFIX);","@@ -209,9 +248,16 @@ public void emit(String emitKey, InputStream inputStream, Metadata userMetadata,","         // CONTENT_ONLY emit keys are the input's own name, so without the extension the output","         // collides with the input. UNPACK keys already carry the embedded file's own name and","         // extension, so appending there would rename every unpacked file.","-        if (parseContext.get(ParseMode.class) == ParseMode.CONTENT_ONLY","-                && !StringUtils.isBlank(config.fileExtension())) {","-            emitKey += \".\" + config.fileExtension();","+        // compression follows the same rule: never gzip an unpacked file under its own name","+        boolean gzip = false;","+        if (parseContext.get(ParseMode.class) == ParseMode.CONTENT_ONLY) {","+            if (!StringUtils.isBlank(config.f